# ADWRKS WordPress → Next.js migration (repo root)

## Routable path index (middleware fast 404)

When you add, remove, or change routable URLs, regenerate the build-time index:

- Hebrew: `web/src/data/content/pages.json`, `posts.json`, `categories.json`, `urls.json`
- English: `web/src/data/content-en/pages.json`, `posts.json`, `categories.json`, `urls.json`
- Redirect sources in `web/next.config.ts` (must stay in sync with `REDIRECT_ALLOWLIST` in `web/src/lib/routing/routable-path-index.ts`)

Run (automatic on `npm run build` in `web/`):

```bash
cd web && node scripts/generate-routable-path-index.mjs
```

Commit the updated `web/src/generated/routable-path-index.json` when path data changes.

## Agency positioning

Follow `.cursor/rules/adwrks-agency-positioning-lock.mdc` — do not leak Website Building positioning globally.

## App conventions

Next.js app lives in `web/`. Read `web/AGENTS.md` before changing routing or Next APIs.
